WEBVTT

1
00:00:05.070 --> 00:00:09.070
Texture compression is another useful thing to consider here.

2
00:00:09.070 --> 00:00:15.470
So by default we're DXT1 and on DX11.

3
00:00:15.470 --> 00:00:21.070
But there are a few different texture compression settings you can choose from.

4
00:00:21.899 --> 00:00:27.100
Again these can be found from double clicking the texture in your content browser

5
00:00:27.100 --> 00:00:31.899
and depending on its use and how you want it to be compressed

6
00:00:31.899 --> 00:00:35.899
there are a series of compression settings here for you to decide.

7
00:00:35.899 --> 00:00:39.899
So whether it's a normal map or if it's a UI element

8
00:00:39.899 --> 00:00:43.899
generally you probably wouldn't want UI elements being compressed as much.

9
00:00:43.899 --> 00:00:50.299
So Unreal is trying to give you some affordances for what this texture is being used for

10
00:00:50.299 --> 00:00:54.700
and therefore under the hood it can decide on the compression of that texture.

11
00:00:55.500 --> 00:00:57.420
And then we've got texture groups as well.

12
00:00:58.380 --> 00:01:04.609
So depending on the level of detail you want inside of your texture

13
00:01:04.609 --> 00:01:10.450
you can group the textures and also when you set them to groups

14
00:01:10.450 --> 00:01:15.730
you can change textures on a per group basis under the hood.

15
00:01:15.730 --> 00:01:21.329
So for example if you say okay group all these textures into this UI element

16
00:01:21.329 --> 00:01:24.129
or group all these textures into the vehicle element

17
00:01:24.129 --> 00:01:27.969
when you're trying to scale settings under the hood

18
00:01:28.689 --> 00:01:32.209
you know that they're being affected for that entire group.

19
00:01:32.209 --> 00:01:35.890
So it's a nice way to kind of set up the group

20
00:01:35.890 --> 00:01:38.930
so that everything's categorized into its own bucket

21
00:01:39.650 --> 00:01:43.329
and then depending what you want to dial up and dial down

22
00:01:43.329 --> 00:01:45.969
those will then affect everything within that group.

23
00:01:45.969 --> 00:01:50.769
So very useful to consider when trying to make these optimizations.
